# the Mach-O image writer: an executable from the image record of a link
#
# every address, file offset and size of a section comes from the layout
# record, and every byte of one from the relocated record, so the writer
# computes no address of the layout. it builds the Mach-O model the Mach-O
# writer turns into bytes. the header takes its cpu type and subtype from the
# architecture's code, the settled capability bits and the traits. a segment
# command maps each segment of the layout under the name of its format's
# segment, page zero below it reaching up to the system's image base, and
# __LINKEDIT after the last. LC_LOAD_DYLINKER names the system's loader,
# LC_BUILD_VERSION the platform of the environment, the oldest version of the
# target or else of the system, and the target's SDK, and LC_MAIN the entry.
# the link-edit data is the rebases, the function starts, the data in code,
# the symbol table and its names, each through its codec, and LC_UUID a hash
# of the image.
#
# an address the image holds is rebased by the loader: through chained
# fixups from the version the system binds through them on, and through
# rebase opcodes before it. a link that needs what the image cannot hold yet
# is refused, naming what it needs.

